A process's description tells PMP_MAX_ENTRIES as the most region slots a process may have,
where the PMP has fewer entries for them, as RP2350's Hazard3 has seven.

Caught-by: fuzz-rp2350
Report: a description differs from the capability it describes
Witness: fuzz-rp2350 describe-every-type

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -931,7 +931,7 @@
     case CAP_PROCESS:
         /* Its region slots, and the most a process may have here, an entry each: what OP_POOL_ALLOC holds a4 to. */
         arg[2] = ((const struct process *)cap_object(cap))->regions;
-        arg[3] = pmp_entry_count;
+        arg[3] = PMP_MAX_ENTRIES;
         break;
     case CAP_NOTIFICATION:
         /* The bits it may signal, never those that are set, which only a wait takes, with RIGHT_R. */
